{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/touring-exhibition/869","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe, A Life Well Lived: Photographs by Malcolm Varon","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","id":"actor/1","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"The exhibition includes prints by Varon, as well as photographs by Alfred Stieglitz, Todd Webb, Tony Vaccaro, and others. These previously unpublished photographs by Malcolm Varon reveal rarely seen aspects of O’Keeffe’s life and personality; her keen sense of humor, her easy smile (and laughter), and her close relationship with Juan Hamilton, the assistant who began working for her in 1973. Also featured are friends and family, including her sister Claudia and O’Keeffe’s beloved Chow Chows. Included alongside these are photographs of O’Keeffe’s Abiquiú House, and the stunning landscapes surrounding it and her Ghost Ranch property.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"Activity"}